  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Food Production and Marketing of High Quality and Safe Maize</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Matembwe AMCOS is primarily a maize growing smallholder farmers&apos; cooperative. The AMCOS being rural and remote is comprised of 685 members of which 347 are mainly women and female youths. These are the main direct beneficiaries although indirectly more people in the households indirectly depend on the AMCOS for livelihoods and employment. The objective of the AMCOS is to increase members incomes and livelihoods through increased maize production, productivity and quality. This will be realized with USADF capacity assistance and technical support to use appropriate fertilizers for farms that will be tested for deficiencies. Also the AMCOS will earn additional income from the carbon market using its 523 acres of forest reserves.</narrative>
  </description>
